</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results and Discussion.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Pooling Strategies. ‣ 4.2 Ablation Studies ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Foley Control: Aligning a Frozen Latent Text-to-Audio Model to Video" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Results and Discussion. ‣ 4.2 Ablation Studies ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Foley Control: Aligning a Frozen Latent Text-to-Audio Model to Video" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the lower-resolution <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Single pooled embedding</span> configuration achieves performance on par with, or slightly better than, the grid8 embedding variant.
Despite a substantial reduction in visual token count—and therefore compute and memory use—no meaningful loss in temporal alignment or perceptual fidelity was observed.
Across 400k training steps, the metrics differ by less than <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.03" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.03</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.03</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that the mid-level spatial resolution of the single-pooled embeddings captures sufficient motion and context cues for Foley synchronization.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="163.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 547.58 163.13" width="547.58"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,163.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(56.9,0) translate(0,38.65) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -56.89 -38.65)"><g class="ltx_nestedsvg" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 0) translate(56.9,0) translate(0,38.65)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#E6E6E6;--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6E6;--ltx-fg-color:#E6E6E6;" color="#E6E6E6" fill="#E6E6E6" stroke="#E6E6E6" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 12.9 0 L 12.9 114.9 M 77.39 0 L 77.39 114.9 M 206.37 0 L 206.37 114.9 M 335.36 0 L 335.36 114.9 M 464.34 0 L 464.34 114.9"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#E6E6E6;--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6E6;--ltx-fg-color:#E6E6E6;" color="#E6E6E6" fill="#E6E6E6" stroke="#E6E6E6" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 13.52 L 490.14 13.52 M 0 47.31 L 490.14 47.31 M 0 81.1 L 490.14 81.1 M 0 114.9 L 490.14 114.9"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-width="0.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 12.9 0 L 12.9 5.91 M 77.39 0 L 77.39 5.91 M 206.37 0 L 206.37 5.91 M 335.36 0 L 335.36 5.91 M 464.34 0 L 464.34 5.91 M 12.9 114.9 L 12.9 108.99 M 77.39 114.9 L 77.39 108.99 M 206.37 114.9 L 206.37 108.99 M 335.36 114.9 L 335.36 108.99 M 464.34 114.9 L 464.34 108.99"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-width="0.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 13.52 L 5.91 13.52 M 0 47.31 L 5.91 47.31 M 0 81.1 L 5.91 81.1 M 0 11